{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-classical-limit-topology-free","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:classical-limit-topology-free","kind":"remark","title":"Topology-free surreal reformulation of the $q\\to1$ limit","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-classical-limit-functor","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-classical-limit-obstruction"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-classical-limit-functor","tags":["classical-limit","surreal","standard-part","q-to-1","topology-free"],"text":"classical-limit-topology-free.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:classical-limit-topology-free\"></a><p><strong>Topology-free reformulation (forward reference).</strong> The <a href=\"#def:classical-limit-functor\" data-at=\"stochastic-mechanics/classical-limit-construction\">classical limit functor</a> uses a topological <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q \\to 1</code> limit on the parameter space, which has obstructions (<a href=\"#def:classical-limit-obstruction\" data-at=\"stochastic-mechanics/classical-limit-construction\">classical limit obstruction</a>). The appendix replaces it with a literal evaluation in Conway's surreal field at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q = 1 + \\varepsilon</code>, then takes the standard-part. Both replacements are conjectural; if they hold, they remove the need for any analytic machinery on the parameter space.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/classical-limit-topology-free.md","heading":"Remark","number":"21.4.6","page":"b/rem-classical-limit-topology-free","qa":{"counts":{"pass":57,"fail":1,"warn":2,"na":17,"unknown":0,"stale":0},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":0}}}
